;Gallery Storyboards declaration. Assigned storyboards are selectable via Gallery Mode
;submenu ('menu.itemname.gallery' parameter in screenpack DEF file)

;Declaring storyboards consists of setting up following parameters:

; - id (required)
;	Set to name that should be stored for use with unlocks paramvalue.
;	This parameter also initiates new storyboard declaration, so it has to be
;	assigned before any other parameter used by the same storyboard.
;	All storyboards should have unique id names.

; - path (required)
;	Set Path to file with def extension (relative to game directory).
;	containing cutscenes events coded in storyboard definition file.
;	https://www.elecbyte.com/mugendocs/storyboard.html

; - previewspr (only used in main gallery screen) [optional]
;	Set groupNo and indexNo to load from sff file defined in "storyboards.spr"
;	system.def [Gallery Info] paramvalue, to show preview sprite for items.
;	If is not defined, "preview.unknown.spr" will be displayed.

; - previewsize (only used in main gallery screen) [optional]
;	Set Width and Height of for gallery preview sprite defined in previewspr paramvalue.
;	If is not defined, "preview.storyboard.size" system.def [Gallery Info] paramvalue will be used.

; - previewpos (only used in main gallery screen) [optional]
;	Set posX and posY for gallery preview sprite which is the same defined in previewspr paramvalue.
;	If is not defined, "preview.storyboard.offset" system.def [Gallery Info] paramvalue will be used.

; - previewspacing (only used in main gallery screen) [optional]
;	Set spacingX and spacingY for gallery preview sprite which is the same defined in previewspr paramvalue.
;	If is not defined, "preview.storyboard.spacing" system.def [Gallery Info] paramvalue will be used.

; - previewscale (only used in main gallery screen) [optional]
;	Set scaleX and scaleY for gallery preview sprite which is the same defined in previewspr paramvalue.
;	If is not defined, "preview.storyboard.scale" system.def [Gallery Info] paramvalue will be used.

; - info (only used in main gallery screen) [optional]
;	Set to description that should be displayed for storyboard selected.
;	If is not defined, "info.unknown.text" system.def [Gallery Info] paramvalue will be used.

; - unlock (optional)
;	Pure Lua code, executed exactly as is, each time upon loading gallery menu.
;	If it evaluates to boolean 'true' the storyboard will be selectable from
;	gallery mode submenu, or hidden on 'false'. Default: true.
;	https://github.com/ikemen-engine/Ikemen-GO/wiki/Lua#content-unlocking

;Examples:

[GalleryStoryboards]
id = Storyboard 1
path = data/kfm/intro.def
previewspr = 1,1
info = Kung Fu Man Motif Introduction.

id = Storyboard 2
path = chars/kfm/intro.def
previewspr = 1,2
info = Introduction Cutscene for KFM's story.

id = Storyboard 3
path = chars/kfm/ending.def
previewspr = 1,3
info = Ending Cutscene for KFM's story.
unlock = stats.modes ~= nil and stats.modes.arcade ~= nil and stats.modes.arcade.clearcount ~= nil and (stats.modes.arcade.clearcount.kfm720 ~= nil or stats.modes.arcade.clearcount.kfmz ~= nil or stats.modes.arcade.clearcount.kfm_zss ~= nil or stats.modes.arcade.clearcount.kfm_zaxis ~= nil)

id = Storyboard 4
path = data/kfm/gameover.def
previewspr = 1,4
info = Game Over Screen.

id = Storyboard 5
path = data/kfm/credits.def
previewspr = 1,5
info = Scrolling Ending Credits.